.TH BCHECK 1.SH NAMEbcheck \- check the brackets in a source file.SH SYNOPSIS\fBbcheck\fR[\-q] [file].SH DESCRIPTION\fBbcheck\fRreads a source file, or the standard input, and prints each line withits number and the count of brackets still open at its end:.nf    00001: 01  int f(){ if (a) { b(); }.fiIf the brackets do not balance at the end of the file it rings the belland says how many are still open:\fBWARNING !!! 1 brackets still open !\fRIt returns 0 either way..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-q\fRquiet: only the warning, not the listing..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOcb, cxref